        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "Now let me solve the problem.\n\n**Problem:** Solve $x^2y''-2xy'-(y')^2=0$ for $x>2$, with $y(3)=\\tfrac12$, $y'(3)=-9$.\n\n**Solution:** Let $p = y'$. Then $y'' = p' = \\frac{dp}{dx}$, giving\n$$x^2 p' - 2xp - p^2 = 0.$$\n\nThis is a Riccati equation. Divide by $x^2$: $p' = \\frac{2p}{x} + \\frac{p^2}{x^2}$.\n\nSubstitute $p = \\frac{1}{u}$ (Bernoulli-type). Then $p' = -\\frac{u'}{u^2}$:\n$$-\\frac{u'}{u^2} = \\frac{2}{xu} + \\frac{1}{x^2u^2} \\implies -u' = \\frac{2u}{x} + \\frac{1}{x^2} \\implies u' + \\frac{2}{x}u = -\\frac{1}{x^2}.$$\n\nIntegrating factor $\\mu = x^2$: $(x^2u)' = -1$, so $x^2u = -x + C$, giving $u = \\frac{C-x}{x^2}$.\n\nThus $p = y' = \\frac{x^2}{C-x}$.\n\nApply $y'(3) = -9$: $\\frac{9}{C-3} = -9 \\implies C-3 = -1 \\implies C = 2$.\n\nSo $y' = \\frac{x^2}{2-x} = -\\frac{x^2}{x-2}$.\n\nIntegrate: $y = -\\int \\frac{x^2}{x-2}dx = -\\int\\left(x+2+\\frac{4}{x-2}\\right)dx = -\\left(\\frac{x^2}{2}+2x+4\\ln(x-2)\\right)+D$.\n\nApply $y(3)=\\tfrac12$: $-\\left(\\frac92+6+4\\ln 1\\right)+D = \\frac12 \\implies -\\frac{21}{2}+D=\\frac12 \\implies D = 11$.\n\nSo $y = -\\frac{x^2}{2}-2x-4\\ln(x-2)+11$.\n\nLet me verify: $y' = -x-2-\\frac{4}{x-2} = \\frac{-(x+2)(x-2)-4}{x-2}=\\frac{-(x^2-4)-4}{x-2}=\\frac{-x^2}{x-2}=\\frac{x^2}{2-x}$. ✓ At $x=3$: $\\frac{9}{-1}=-9$. ✓",
        "tool_calls": [
          {
            "id": "call_5d7c989ed43b4f9da45e448b",
            "index": 0,
            "type": "function",
            "function": {
              "name": "submit_solution",
              "arguments": "{\"region_id\": \"region_art_0002_01\", \"final_answer\": \"y = -\\\\frac{x^2}{2} - 2x - 4\\\\ln(x-2) + 11, \\\\quad x>2\", \"reasoning\": \"方程 x^2y''-2xy'-(y')^2=0 中不显含 y，属可降阶的二阶非线性方程，令 p=y'，则 y''=p'，方程化为 x^2p'-2xp-p^2=0，即 p'=(2p)/x+p^2/x^2（Riccati 方程）。\\n\\n作代换 p=1/u，则 p'=-u'/u^2，代入得 -u'/u^2=2/(xu)+1/(x^2u^2)，整理得线性方程 u'+(2/x)u=-1/x^2。\\n\\n积分因子 μ=x^2，得 (x^2u)'=-1，故 x^2u=-x+C，即 u=(C-x)/x^2，从而 p=y'=x^2/(C-x)。\\n\\n由 y'(3)=-9：9/(C-3)=-9，得 C-3=-1，C=2，故 y'=x^2/(2-x)=-x^2/(x-2)。\\n\\n积分：y=-∫x^2/(x-2)dx=-∫(x+2+4/(x-2))dx=-(x^2/2+2x+4ln(x-2))+D。\\n\\n由 y(3)=1/2：-(9/2+6+0)+D=1/2，得 D=11。\\n\\n故解为 y=-x^2/2-2x-4ln(x-2)+11。验证：y'=-x-2-4/(x-2)=-x^2/(x-2)，在 x=3 处为 -9，且 y(3)=1/2，满足初值条件。\"}"
